1
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:07,750
This video shows you how to follow one record from its original text to what arrived.

2
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:11,630
You're in firewall-parse, the pipeline that feeds siem.

3
00:00:11,680 --> 00:00:15,508
To see real records, capture some from its source.

4
00:00:15,508 --> 00:00:19,170
Choose Sample, Add sample, then Capture.

5
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:23,755
The capture target is the source, firewall.

6
00:00:23,755 --> 00:00:24,670
Start it.

7
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:27,561
A capture copies records as they arrive.

8
00:00:27,561 --> 00:00:30,362
The pipeline goes on as before.

9
00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:34,534
Use these records.

10
00:00:34,534 --> 00:00:38,830
The pipeline runs on them here, and sends nothing anywhere.

11
00:00:38,880 --> 00:00:40,799
Each row is one record.

12
00:00:40,799 --> 00:00:45,470
The struck-out text is _raw, the original firewall line.

13
00:00:45,470 --> 00:00:47,750
The last step removed it.

14
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:48,836
Open a record.

15
00:00:48,836 --> 00:00:52,471
Green fields are what the pipeline added.

16
00:00:56,880 --> 00:01:01,817
Open the removed fields, to read the original line beside the others.

17
00:01:02,160 --> 00:01:06,277
To see a record partway through, pause it after a step.

18
00:01:06,277 --> 00:01:08,190
Pause after the parser.

19
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:13,625
_raw is still there, next to the fields the parser read from it.

20
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:17,983
Move the pause to the rename step.

21
00:01:17,983 --> 00:01:20,720
user is now user.name.

22
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:28,310
Clear the pause to see the whole pipeline again.

23
00:01:28,360 --> 00:01:30,239
Check on learning.

24
00:01:30,439 --> 00:01:34,866
How do you see a record as it was after the second step?

25
00:01:39,266 --> 00:01:43,543
Pause the records after that step, with its pause button.

26
00:01:44,443 --> 00:01:48,195
Next, find which step changed a field.
